digraph decision {
  rankdir=TB;
  bgcolor="#0d0e12";
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, fillcolor="#181a20", color="#343846", fontcolor="#e2e8f0"];
  edge [color="#3b82f6", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, fontcolor="#93c5fd"];

  history [
    label="1. Prior-journal learning pass (python3 scripts/stats.py at 2026-10-30T08:46Z)\nSettled: 2 WIN, 4 LOSS, 3 EXPIRED with pct, 2 EXPIRED never filled. Sum +4.95%, win rate 33.3%,\navg win +1.51%, avg loss -1.22%. n=11 terminal, mixed setups: no directional inference taken.\nLessons checked against that folder's own review.md / trade.toml / decision_tree.dot and used here:\n- LOSS-1.50%_2026-10-23T1147Z_ZECUSDT (LONG limit 1203, SL 1185): filled 22:30Z and stopped at 22:35Z,\nlosing inside the same 5-minute candle, because the stop sat inside the structure being tested.\n-> today the stop is 734.00, one full percent (about 1.2x hourly ATR) ABOVE the 726.84 crash-hour high,\nnot just above the entry zone.\n- LOSS-1.30%_2026-10-19T1533Z_XRPUSDT (SHORT limit 1.3065, SL 1.3235): faded before a squeeze, stop sat\ninside the squeeze reach, and a resumption-style impulse took it out.\n-> today the same risk exists on the resumption headline (Jev: a short is more exposed to a resumption spike\nthan a long is to a bad post-mortem = 0.70), which is why the stop is at 734 and not 727, and why the expiry\nstops at 02:00Z instead of running through the end of the guided 48h band.\n- EXPIRED_2026-10-18T1730Z_AVAXUSDT (never touched) and EXPIRED_2026-10-28T0840Z_ZECUSDT (never touched):\nfill probability must be carried separately, and an unfilled order pays 0.\n-> P(fill) 0.56 is used explicitly; EV/order = 0.56 x EV/fill, no-fill branch at 0.\n- EXPIRED+1.14%_ZECUSDT, EXPIRED+1.73%_UNIUSDT, EXPIRED+3.95%_ASTERUSDT: non-TP exits are often partial\ngains, so the expiry branch is real and was measured (P(expiry close below entry | neither) = 0.82).\n- EXPIRED+3.95%_2026-10-18T1535Z_ASTERUSDT: the TP was put at a range extreme (0.721) and price peaked 0.7190,\nso the target was never filled and the trade expired +3.95% untargeted.\n-> here TP 694.00 sits INSIDE the measured 692-698 support cluster, not at the 680 extreme, and Jev preferred\n694 over holding for 680 (0.79).\n- WIN+1.26%_2026-10-27T0919Z_ASTERUSDT: selling into measured supply after a rejection, with the stop beyond\nthe regime extreme, is the one setup shape in this journal that has worked; today's ticket is built the same way.\nProcess lesson: the two PENDING folders (CAKE 2026-10-25, BTC 2026-10-29) are NOT used as evidence here.\n"
    fillcolor="#1e293b" color="#3b82f6"
  ];

  extract [
    label="2. Chart extraction (image 261030_09h43m21s_screenshot.png, BNBUSDT 1h, Aster)\nFooter 09:43:20 UTC+1 = 2026-10-30T08:43:20Z; last price 705.58 (-2.21, -0.31%).\n705 hourly closes extracted from the pixels: x-axis day ticks 1..31 then Nov (Oct 1 - Oct 30) with\nx(day) spacing 57.87 px and 2.41 px/hour; y-axis gridlines 812 (y=59) .. 688 (y=997), 7.565 px per unit,\ncross-checked against the dashed last-price line which lands exactly on 705.58.\nValidation: extraction vs Binance 1h closes over all 705 bars, mean +0.39, median +0.38, sd ~1.40 units\n(~0.19%). Resolution limit: the plotted line is closes only, so wicks are invisible; the true 680.00 low\nnever appears in the image (extracted low close 698.25).\nMeasured structure: monthly high 800.8 (Oct 4 19:00Z); Oct 18 low 708.5; recovery to 751.1 (Oct 21);\n10-day range 708.5 - 760.4 to Oct 29; Oct 28 10:00Z high 760.4; Oct 29 15:00Z pivot high 750.2;\ncollapse to 698.2 close (Oct 29 23:00Z); bounce to 722.08 (Oct 30 05:00Z); fade back to 705.6.\nExchange klines (used for wick structure, verified against the chart): crash hour 744.90 -> L 680.00 ->\nC 698.00 on 137,383 BNB; follow-through lows 692.00 and 682.16; three rejections at 719.94 / 720.00 /\n722.08; crash-hour rebound high 726.84. ATR(14) on hourly closes 6.05 = 0.86%; ATR(24) 4.50 = 0.64%.\n680 is a single-venue print: Bybit perp 676.40, Bybit spot 678.14, MEXC 679.00, Aster spot 684.00.\n"
    fillcolor="#0f2a43" color="#38bdf8"
  ];

  scen [
    label="3. Scenarios - jev_decide, pre-research then post-research (bounded choice, readable as a distribution)\nPre-research: base 0.58, pop-then-fade 0.19, sweep-lows-then-bounce 0.18, continuation 0.02, V-recovery 0.00.\nPost-research (reselected, confidence 0.35 - contested):\n  base_chop, hourly closes 690-722, no dislodging headline: 0.42\n  continuation_down, new low under 680: 0.22   (was 0.02 before the incident was known)\n  sweep_lows_then_bounce (dip 680-694 then back to 705-715): 0.16\n  pop_then_fade (rally into 715-722 then back to 690-700): 0.09   (was 0.19)\n  headline_override (>3% in one or two hours on news): 0.10\n  v_recovery (reclaim 722 and run to 726-745): 0.00\nReading: the modal picture is a two-sided base after a liquidation event, tilted slightly DOWN once the\nvenue-risk evidence is included. Not one dominant scenario; the ticket does not need one.\n\nLevel / ordering probabilities (jev_noul, separate overlapping propositions - never summed):\n24h: >=715 0.66 | >=722 0.57 | <=698 0.64 | <=692 0.47 | <=680 0.24 | close higher in 24h 0.50 |\n     hourly closes confined to 690-722 0.51 | touch 715 before 698 0.57 | 716 before 692 0.52\n36h: >=715 0.74 | >=722 0.67 | <=692 0.48 | >=730 0.25 | <=676 0.28\n12h: >=715 0.65 | <=698 0.49\nStructural: 716-722 rejects rather than gets reclaimed 0.72; the 708-712 broken floor dominates a rally 0.54;\nthe 29 Oct crash is capitulation rather than a first leg 0.63; 'fading 715-720 is better supported than\nbuying 690-696' 0.60; 'a 692 entry carries material asymmetric risk because the 680 low is a single-venue\nprint' 0.80; 'the setup is still valid at 706' 0.81.\n"
    fillcolor="#1e1b4b" color="#8b5cf6"
  ];

  research [
    label="4. Research (Jev-defined agenda only; full dated log in research_log.txt)\nGate: off-chart information could materially change the forecast or the decision = 0.83.\nAgenda jev_decide: event_dominance 0.71 > downside_tail 0.17 > upside_reclaim 0.06 > correlated 0.02.\nQuestion asked: is a BNB-specific or venue-specific occurrence scheduled or announced inside\n2026-10-30T09:00Z - 2026-10-31T21:00Z; what caused the 20:00Z candle; live price/candle anchor.\nFindings that changed the forecast: Binance security incident (official 2026-10-30T02:23:22Z): compromised\nDevOps laptop, unauthorised withdrawals, no private-key leak, ~$6.3B impact, ~$3B frozen, SAFU covers,\ndeposits and withdrawals suspended. Withdrawals guided to resume 'in the next 48 hours' from\n2026-10-30T04:21Z (band to 2026-10-31T04:21Z, no exact time). Post-mortem and Proof of Reserves pending\nand undated. The crash was broad-market but BNB-specific in size (ETH -3.38%, BTC -2.47%, BNB -6.30% in the\nsame hour; ~$600-628M liquidated, longs dominant). Standard Chartered expects more downside until assets\nare unfrozen. Bounce volume decayed to 14-31k BNB/h against 137k on the break (no absorption).\nCleared: no burn (37th burn done 2026-10-19), no unlock schedule, no BNB pair in the 30 Oct /BTC delistings,\nno crypto maintenance, BNB Chain mainnet not in window, no calendared legal date.\nNot found: exact resumption timestamp, whether the post-mortem lands in the window, whether BNB is in scope\nof the 30 Oct margin-tier update. Net effect: upside tail stays small (P(>=730 in 36h) 0.25) while the\ndownside continuation scenario quadrupled versus the chart-only read; the fade thesis survived.\n"
    fillcolor="#14261c" color="#22c55e"
  ];

  candS [
    label="5. CAND S (selected): SHORT LIMIT 716.00 / TP 694.00 / SL 734.00 / expire 2026-10-31T02:00Z\nEntry 716.00 = lower third of the 715-722 supply that rejected three times (719.94 / 720.00 / 722.08);\n  Jev P(fill) 0.56 in 17h (0.65 in 24h); preferred over 718.00 (fill 0.41) and 719.00 (fill 0.42) at 0.70.\nTP 694.00 = inside the 692-698 support cluster, above the 680-682 crash lows; Jev prefers it over 680 at 0.79.\nSL 734.00 = 1.0% (about 1.2x hourly ATR) above the 726.84 crash-hour rebound high; SL-first only 0.08;\n  Jev rates 727 as 'too close to 726.84' at 0.73 and 730 as a 'thin buffer' at 0.73, so 734 was chosen.\nG +3.07263% | L -2.51397% | RR 1.222 | p_BE 0.45 | p_TP 0.80 | EV/fill +2.25698% | EV/order +1.26391%\nSensitivity EV/order: 0.72/0.16 -> +1.01363%; 0.65/0.20 -> +0.83687%; 0.60/0.25, fill 0.50 -> +0.60754%;\n  0.55/0.30, fill 0.45 -> +0.42109%. Positive in every case, so the decision does not hinge on Jev's 0.80.\nNeither branch (0.12) valued at 0 in the base EV even though P(expiry close below 716 | neither) = 0.82.\n"
    fillcolor="#272015" color="#eab308"
  ];

  candL [
    label="6. CAND L (evaluated independently, rejected on structure and on relative economics)\nLONG LIMIT 692.00 / TP 712.00 / SL 676.00 / 2026-10-31T02:00Z: p_BE 0.4444, p_TP 0.63 -> EV/order +0.64624%.\nLONG LIMIT 692.00 / TP 714.00 / SL 675.00 (24h): p_BE 0.4359, p_TP 0.52 -> EV/order +0.23699%.\nLONG LIMIT 686.00 / TP 712.00 / SL 674.00: p_fill 0.36, EV/order +0.50694%.\nWhy rejected: it is positive but strictly worse than the short on every measured dimension - lower EV/order,\nlower structural support (Jev: the premise that the single-venue 680 low holds is materially risky at 0.80),\nand it fights the post-research tilt (continuation_down 0.22 is exactly the scenario that fills the 692 limit\nand then keeps going). Jev: 'fading 715-720 is better supported than buying 690-696' = 0.60.\nAlso rejected: MARKET SHORT 705.60/690.00/716.00 (p_TP 0.48 vs p_BE 0.40 -> EV/order +0.29478%, no\nstructural entry) and MARKET LONG 705.60/720.00/694.00 (p_TP 0.40 vs p_BE 0.4462 -> EV/order NEGATIVE).\n"
    fillcolor="#2a1818" color="#ef4444"
  ];

  forecast [
    label="7. Independent forecast (drawn in chart_prediction.svg and in graphpoints.csv rows 09:00Z..02:00Z)\nModal path, contested: chop 704-710 through the European morning -> afternoon push into the 715-718 supply\n  (this is where the 716 limit fills) -> rejection -> evening and overnight fade 708 -> 701 -> 696 -> 693.5\n  around 00:00Z (TP 694 tagged) -> small bounce to 697.0 at expiry 2026-10-31T02:00Z.\nWhy this shape: base_chop 0.42 plus pop_then_fade 0.09, with P(716 before 692) = 0.52 (barely up first) and\nP(696 before 722) style ordering; the path does not reach 680 or 722 and so does not need any tail scenario.\nContested markers carried explicitly: continuation_down 0.22 would instead break 690-680 (the forecast would\nbe wrong and the stop at 734 untouched, TP reached faster); sweep_lows_then_bounce 0.16 would dip first and\ntag 692 before the rally (the limit at 716 would then fill late or not at all); headline_override 0.10 can\ninvalidate the whole level map in one or two hours. The forecast was written before the ticket levels were\nfixed and was not bent to them; it is the modal path, and it happens to touch entry then TP.\n"
    fillcolor="#2a2338" color="#c084fc"
  ];

  checks [
    label="8. Contradictions, robustness and validation\n- Conflict recorded, not hidden: '694 before 727' = 0.58 asked over 24h but 0.72 asked over 17h. The longer\n  window cannot make a target-first outcome less likely, so one of the two is wrong; both are far above the\n  selected ticket's p_BE of 0.45 and the sensitivity table uses the lower end, so it does not flip the decision.\n- 'SL 730 better risk-adjusted than SL 727' = 0.32 (i.e. Jev prefers 727) while the three-way EVs prefer the\n  wider stop. Resolved structurally, not by counting: 727 is contradicted by the requirement 'stop beyond a\n  measured structural extreme' (it sits 0.16 under the 726.84 high) and 734 clears it by 1.0% (about 1.2 ATR).\n- Wide-stop trap checked: EV is not manufactured by widening. At 734 the target is 22 points and the risk 18,\n  RR 1.22, p_BE 0.45; the measured p_TP would have to fall below 0.45 (from 0.80, or below 0.58 on the most\n  pessimistic reading) to make it EV-negative.\n- Headline-risk asymmetry (Jev 0.70 that a short is more exposed to a resumption spike than a long to a bad\n  post-mortem) is real and is the main reason the ticket is capped at 17h/expiry 02:00Z rather than 36h and\n  why the stop is 2.5% away rather than 1.5%.\n- NO_TRADE case tested directly: 'the correct action is NO_TRADE because the headline dominates' = 0.23.\n  Scenario distribution is contested (decide confidence 0.35) but every candidate was costed; rejecting a\n  positive-EV ticket because the scenario set is mixed would be a preference, not evidence.\n- Re-anchor 2026-10-30T08:59Z: Binance spot 705.66, perp 705.40, Aster perp 705.39 against chart 705.58\n  (+0.01%); no level needed to move; setup-valid-at-live-price 0.81.\n- Final battery jev_decide: short_716_694_734 1.00 with all three requirements supported (positive\n  expectancy, explicit fill probability, stop beyond a measured extreme); reject 0.00, market short 0.00,\n  long 0.00. Treated as a parameter confirmation only - the arithmetic and the level choice are mine.\n- Model limits stated: no fees/funding/slippage in this journal; SL fills at its level on touch (no gap\n  slippage), so a headline spike through 734 costs exactly -2.51397% and no more.\n"
    fillcolor="#2d1b24" color="#f43f5e"
  ];

  terminal [
    label="FINAL: GO LIMIT (PENDING)\nBNBUSDT SHORT LIMIT 716.00 | TP 694.00 (+3.07263%) | SL 734.00 (-2.51397%) | RR 1.222\nP(fill 17h) 0.56 | P(TP before SL | fill) 0.80 | p_BE 0.45 | EV/fill +2.25698% | EV/order +1.26391%\nPlace 2026-10-30T09:00Z | Expire 2026-10-31T02:00Z\n"
    shape=ellipse fillcolor="#1e293b" color="#eab308" fontcolor="#fef08a"
  ];

  history -> extract; extract -> scen; scen -> research; research -> candS; research -> candL;
  candS -> forecast; candL -> forecast [style=dashed color="#ef4444" label="rejected"];
  candS -> checks; candL -> checks [style=dashed color="#ef4444"];
  forecast -> checks; checks -> terminal;
}